  explain <KOID> [DB]    Explain an object (provenance + evidence)
  index [DB]             Storage/index statistics
  schema [DB]            List types in the knowledge base
  import <SOURCE> [ARGS]  Import from DB (postgres, pgvector, sqlite, mongodb, neo4j)
  ingest-dir [PATH] [DB] [--parallel] [--incremental] [--model-dir DIR] Ingest directory into knowledge base
  report [PATH]          Print knowledge report for directory
  model install [MODEL]  Install an embedding model into the local store (offline use)
  hash-password PASSWORD Print an argon2id hash for [auth].users (aikoql.toml)

Server options (serve mode):
  --listen ADDR          TCP listen address (e.g., 127.0.0.1:9090; empty host = loopback)
  --native-port ADDR     D-15 framed native protocol listener (loopback-only; requires --tcp-token)
  --tcp-token SPEC       TCP auth: TOKEN[:TENANT[:ROLE1,ROLE2]] (repeatable, required with --listen)
                         (dev-only: tokens hit the process list — set AIKOQL_TCP_TOKEN or
                         AIKOQL_TCP_TOKEN_FILE in production instead; env replaces flags)
  --metrics-addr ADDR    HTTP metrics + health endpoint (e.g., 127.0.0.1:9091)
  --embedding-provider P  Embedding provider: "candle" (default), "http", or "ollama"
  --embedding-base-url U  OpenAI-compatible base URL (default: http://localhost:11434)
  --embedding-model M     Model name (default: nomic-embed-text)
  --embedding-api-key K   API key for remote endpoints (omit for Ollama)
  --model-dir DIR         Local embedding model store (default: ~/.aikoql/models)
  --config PATH           TOML config file (auto: ./aikoql.toml, then /etc/aikoql/aikoql.toml)

Precedence: defaults < aikoql.toml < env (AIKOQL_*) < CLI flags.
HTTP auth: [auth] users/session_ttl_seconds in aikoql.toml (argon2id hashes);
  AIKOQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD bootstraps an admin when no users are configured.
  The HTTP/metrics surface is loopback-only unless allow_remote_http = true
